import{_ as a,o as t,c as n,a3 as s}from"./chunks/framework.DOLRlNb_.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"The admin area","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"docs/admin.md","filePath":"docs/admin.md"}'),i={name:"docs/admin.md"};function r(o,e,h,d,l,c){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="the-admin-area" tabindex="-1">The admin area <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-admin-area" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The admin area&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The admin area is where the maintainer looks after the catalog, the accounts and the server&#39;s settings. It is a section of the website under <code>/admin</code> (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/26" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#26</a>). It never shows workouts or health data.</p><p>This page holds the rules: who can do what, and what happens when they do. How the server enforces them is in <a href="./admin-internals">Admin internals</a>.</p><h2 id="who-can-open-it" tabindex="-1">Who can open it <a class="header-anchor" href="#who-can-open-it" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Who can open it&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Admin is a role on the account, either member or admin. Nobody can ask for it (<a href="./adr/0020-every-credential-resolves-to-one-caller">ADR 0020</a>). There is one admin for now and no finer rights.</p><p>An admin reaches the area only by signing in on the website. The phone app, a personal access token and third-party apps never reach it, even for an admin.</p><p>A member who tries to sign in on the website is signed out at once with the usual &quot;wrong email or password&quot;. The sign-in never reveals an account&#39;s role.</p><h2 id="making-the-first-admin" tabindex="-1">Making the first admin <a class="header-anchor" href="#making-the-first-admin" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Making the first admin&quot;">​</a></h2><p>An admin is made at deploy time, never from the website. The maintainer sets <code>ADMIN_EMAIL</code> (<a href="./releasing#deploy-the-server">Releasing</a>) and the confirmed account with that address becomes an admin when the server starts. An address with no confirmed account does nothing, so signing up first with someone else&#39;s address can&#39;t take the role. The promotion is recorded in the audit log.</p><h2 id="accounts" tabindex="-1">Accounts <a class="header-anchor" href="#accounts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Accounts&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Accounts</strong> screen lists accounts with email, role, confirmation, sign-in status and creation date. You can filter, sort, page and open an account by id. The view lives in the address, so it can be bookmarked (<a href="./web-app#navigation-lives-in-the-url">navigation</a>).</p><p>An admin can:</p><ul><li><strong>Disable</strong> an account. It can&#39;t sign in and every device is signed out. <strong>Enable</strong> reverses it. A disabled account gets the same &quot;wrong email or password&quot; as any other refusal.</li><li><strong>Confirm email</strong> for an unconfirmed account, in its side panel (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/382" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#382</a>). Use it when the email never arrived, or when running locally with no mail server (<a href="./the-api#trying-it-locally">Trying it locally</a>). It has the same effect as the person following the link. A dialog first says the admin vouches for an address nobody proved. The server side is done; the button comes once its mockup is agreed.</li><li><strong>Delete</strong> an account after typing its email again. This removes the account and all its data, exactly as when a user deletes their own account.</li></ul><p>An admin can&#39;t disable or delete their own account.</p><h2 id="settings" tabindex="-1">Settings <a class="header-anchor" href="#settings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Settings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Settings</strong> screen changes the email from-address without a deploy.</p><ul><li><strong>Only non-secret settings are editable here.</strong> The mail server&#39;s host, user and password are set at deploy time and never shown (<a href="./deploying-the-server">Deploying the server</a>).</li><li><strong>A saved from-address replaces the default</strong> from the next email. Both <code>hello@example.com</code> and <code>Coach Poulpy &lt;hello@example.com&gt;</code> work. Anything else is refused and nothing is saved.</li><li><strong>Send test email</strong> sends a message to the signed-in admin and says whether the mail server accepted it.</li></ul><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Status&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>Status</strong> screen shows whether mail works and who is waiting to confirm. It is read-only (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/340" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#340</a>).</p><ul><li><strong>Mail</strong> says whether a mail server is set up and, if so, how the last email went: its kind (confirmation, password reset or test), when, and whether it worked. A server restart forgets it. The mail server&#39;s details are never shown.</li><li><strong>Pending registrations</strong> are accounts whose email isn&#39;t confirmed, newest first, the last 100. Each row shows the address, when it signed up and when its latest link expires. To confirm one, open the account in <a href="#accounts">Accounts</a>.</li></ul><p>The public <code>/status</code> page of the web app is separate. Anyone can open it. It says only whether Coach Poulpy is up or down, never how the server is configured.</p><h2 id="catalog" tabindex="-1">Catalog <a class="header-anchor" href="#catalog" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Catalog&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The server keeps the exercise catalog in two forms: a <strong>catalog draft</strong> the admin edits, and <strong>published revisions</strong> that phones download. Each exercise has its own numbered revisions, so publishing touches only the exercises it names (<a href="./adr/0030-the-catalog-changes-by-exercise-revision-not-by-catalog-version">ADR 0030</a>). The first start seeds both from the catalog the server was built with.</p><p>The admin has an exercise list at <code>/admin/catalog</code> and an editor at <code>/admin/catalog/&lt;slug&gt;</code>. Publishing and retiring are in the list&#39;s selection menu (<a href="https://github.com/tkint/coach-poulpy/issues/338" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">#338</a>).</p><ul><li><strong>Every text is written per language.</strong> Saving needs the English name. Other languages can wait, but publishing needs English and French.</li><li><strong>A slug can change only until the exercise is first published.</strong> Workouts point at it, so after that a rename is refused (<a href="./adr/0008-curated-catalog-with-stable-slugs">ADR 0008</a>).</li><li><strong>Exercises are retired, never deleted.</strong> A retired exercise can be offered again.</li><li><strong>Publishing</strong> gives each named exercise its next revision, or every exercise with a change when none is named. It is refused when a translation is missing or when nothing has changed. Phones see the new revisions at once.</li></ul><p>An exercise&#39;s <strong>change</strong> since its latest published revision is added, edited, retired, offered or none. Its <strong>lifecycle</strong> is active, retiring (retired in the draft, not yet in a published revision) or retired. A preview lists what publishing would do, with each edited field before and after.</p><h2 id="the-audit-log" tabindex="-1">The audit log <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-audit-log" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The audit log&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Every admin write is recorded: who did it, what, and the target. The first screen of the admin shows the last 100 entries. Entries stay when the admin&#39;s own account is deleted, and an entry with no author means the server did it, as at start-up.</p><p>Targets never hold an address in clear. An account is recorded by its id, and an email by its masked form (<code>a***@example.com</code>). Confirming an email by hand is the one account action recorded by masked address rather than id. A password is never recorded.</p>',29)])])}const m=a(i,[["render",r]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
